# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY called node_modules and nothing else. A
# symlink called node_modules — which is what a linked local dependency is, and
# what several package managers create — is not a directory, so the pattern
# misses it and the link gets committed. That has happened on this codebase
# once already: a symlink pointing at its own parent went into a commit, and
# every checkout afterwards failed with ELOOP.
node_modules

# The build. Nothing serves it — `run.sh` runs Vite — and a checked-in copy is
# a second answer to "what does this page say", which disagrees with the first
# the moment somebody edits `page/`. Three separate afternoons on this codebase
# were spent on a stale `dist` answering 200.
dist

# This app's own store: the journeys, their steps, their prose, and every edit
# made to them here. It is decided material — somebody wrote it — and it belongs
# to the machine the app runs on rather than to whichever repository this
# directory happens to be sitting in today. `seed/` beside it is different: that
# is the material this app ships WITH, and it is tracked.
data
